WEIRD Package Registry

The community package registry for the WEIRD programming language.

This repository is intended to host public WEIRD package releases and document how packages are distributed and maintained. Packages are distributed through GitHub Releases rather than a dedicated package server.

Status

The registry is in its early stages. Package discovery and installation require a compatible version of the WEIRD Package Manager (WPM). Until the registry contains published packages and end-to-end compatibility has been verified, functionality should be considered experimental.

Package Distribution

Packages are distributed as versioned GitHub Releases. Each release must contain the archive and metadata required by the compatible WPM client.

The registry identifier is:

github://mic3ul/weird-packages

This identifier is intended for WPM versions that support the GitHub registry adapter.

Publishing Packages

Package maintainers should:

1. Follow the package manifest and archive format specified by the WEIRD documentation.
2. Use a unique package name and a valid semantic version.
3. Test the package in a clean environment before publishing.
4. Publish a GitHub Release containing the required package archive and metadata.
5. Document dependencies and provide a license for the package.

Publishing requires write access to this repository. Never include credentials, access tokens, private keys, or personal information in package archives.

Security

Packages may contain executable code. Review package contents and source before installing or running them.

This registry does not currently guarantee package safety or provide package signing, automated malware scanning, or individual publisher accounts. Integrity checks can detect file modifications but cannot establish that a package is trustworthy.

Contributing

Contributions to registry documentation and package conventions are welcome. Report package issues with the package name, version, and a clear description of the problem.

